 "_readme": "Days above each city's own extreme-heat thresholds. Thresholds are AEMET's OWN RULE, not ours: the 90th/95th/99th percentile of July and August daily maxima, 1971-2000, per station. Verified by reproducing AEMET's published figures exactly (Madrid 36.4 C, Seville 41.2 C).",
 "why_not_35c": "A flat 35 C threshold is not usable across cities and is not a standard. Measured 2011-2025 it yields 0.5 days a year in Barcelona and 66.8 in Seville, a 130-fold spread, so it would call an ordinary Seville day extreme and miss real extremes further north. ETCCDI's standard hot-day index is SU at 25 C, which nearly every Spanish summer day clears. AEMET's percentile rule is locally calibrated and is theirs to defend.",
